From 7bf79465d0338204b2996925832df366224d1d4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:38:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10692/11362] Record that r11l's progress is unobservable, with
 a decision point

The cd82/r11l run has been on its first game for 8h56m against ls20's 7h19m and
wa30's 6h31m, and r11l itself previously finished in 2121 actions.

Liveness is not the question and was checked: ~674% CPU on the worker, ~20 t/s, and
llama-server /slots reports slot 1 is_processing true on two samples 25s apart.

The gap is that nothing exposes the action count mid-run. The per-game row carrying
actions, levels and trajectory_supervisor is written only when a game ends, so
"advancing slowly through a 2500-action budget" and "looping on induction that never
returns an answer" are indistinguishable from outside. Same class as the supervisor
being silent by construction, and it recurs on every long game until a mid-run
progress signal exists.

The loop hypothesis is not idle. The completed ls20/wa30 run returned reasoning_only
24 of 24 completions with chars_final 0 on both games, which exp5798 already
diagnosed as qwen_channel_failure_not_competence_failure. If that repeats here the
induction tier is contributing nothing again and the run is re-measuring the non-LLM
path at a cost of nine hours and counting.

No intervention now, because the 2500-action budget bounds the game. A decision point
is recorded instead so this does not drift: if the partial has not landed by
2026-09-02 03:00Z, treat it as pathological rather than slow, kill the run, keep the
partial, and read completions_consumed first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
